content:
Brief a meeting when it has at least one attendee besides the user and has not been declined by everyone else. That is the whole test — a meeting with another human in it is one you can walk into unprepared.

Skip, silently:
- blocks with no other attendee: focus time, travel, holds, anything the user has put on their own calendar to protect the hour;
- recurring meetings when the 'skip_recurring' setting is on, unless the attendee list has changed since the last occurrence — a new face in a standing meeting is exactly when a brief earns its place;
- meetings the user declined, and ones cancelled after the brief window opened;
- anything starting within the lead time at the moment the job runs, which would arrive after the user is already in the room.

Never brief a meeting twice. A meeting whose time moves forward gets one corrected brief, sent once, saying the time changed.
